  "result": "New object ref each render. Inline object prop = new ref = re-render.\n\n**Fix:** Memoize object with `useMemo`:\n\n```jsx\nconst options = useMemo(() => ({ foo: 'bar' }), []);\n<MyComponent options={options} />\n```\n\nOr memoize component with `React.memo`:\n\n```jsx\nconst MyComponent = React.memo(({ options }) => { ... });\n```\n\nOr move object outside component if static:\n\n```jsx\nconst OPTIONS = { foo: 'bar' }; // outside, no re-create\n\nfunction Parent() {\n  return <MyComponent options={OPTIONS} />;\n}\n```\n\nRoot cause: `{}` === `{}` is `false` in JS. New render = new object = new ref = child sees \"changed\" prop.\n\nBest fix: move static objects out. `useMemo` for derived/dynamic objects. `React.memo` only helps when props are stable refs.",
